From: Jeff Yeung <neojohnson@gmail.com>
Subject: media: ipu6: Restore driver data checks in ISYS runtime PM callbacks

Commit 312c74e6d360 ("media: ipu6: Remove redundant driver data checks")
dropped the NULL checks on dev_get_drvdata() in isys_runtime_pm_suspend()
and isys_runtime_pm_resume(), reasoning that probe() always sets the
driver data. Runtime PM is enabled for the ISYS auxiliary device in
ipu6_bus_initialize_device(), before any driver is bound, and nothing
guarantees that the runtime PM callbacks cannot run while dev->driver is
set but the driver data is not (yet, or any longer) set. On a Dell XPS 13
9340 the suspend callback is reached at the moment ipu6_pci_probe()
finishes, before isys_probe() has stored its driver data, about one boot
in three:

  BUG: kernel NULL pointer dereference, address: 000000000000031c
  Workqueue: pm pm_runtime_work
  RIP: 0010:_raw_spin_lock_irqsave+0x27/0x50
  Call Trace:
   isys_runtime_pm_suspend+0x20/0x100 [intel_ipu6_isys]
   bus_pm_runtime_suspend+0x12/0x40 [intel_ipu6]
   __rpm_callback+0x57/0x200
   rpm_suspend+0x4bb/0x850
   pm_runtime_work+0x98/0xb0

Afterwards the device is stuck in runtime PM state "suspending", the
camera is unusable until reboot, processes opening it hang in D state in
rpm_resume(), and system suspend can hang on them. Seen with kernels 7.0
to 7.2.15 (IPU6 8086:7d19, OV02C10 behind IVSC); kernel 6.18, which still
has the checks, is not affected.

Restore the checks: a runtime PM callback that runs without driver data
has nothing to do and returns 0.

Fixes: 312c74e6d360 ("media: ipu6: Remove redundant driver data checks")
Link: https://github.com/omacom/omarchy-pkgs/issues/2274
Signed-off-by: Jeff Yeung <neojohnson@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys.c b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys.c
--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys.c
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys.c
@@ -858,6 +858,10 @@
 	unsigned long flags;
 	int ret;
 
+	/* Runtime PM can run before isys_probe() has set drvdata */
+	if (!isys)
+		return 0;
+
 	ret = ipu6_mmu_hw_init(adev->mmu);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
@@ -885,6 +889,10 @@
 	struct ipu6_isys *isys = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	unsigned long flags;
 
+	/* Runtime PM can run before isys_probe() has set drvdata */
+	if (!isys)
+		return 0;
+
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&isys->power_lock, flags);
 	isys->power = 0;
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&isys->power_lock, flags);
-- 
